{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colour vector (in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition()"},{"type":"text","text":" sides (left 0), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colours beside a triangle."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/Coloring","text":"Coloring","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First fit in index order (the lexicographically first proper colouring of all) when it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already optimal. Otherwise each vertex in turn takes the least colour its prefix still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"extends with (k-colouring’s self-reduction to its decision problem): a Kempe swap of the last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colouring found when one avoids the prefix, else DSatur branch and bound over the parts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after the prefix that the vertex touches (on sparse components with conflict-directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backjumping and restarts). Khuller and Vazirani show the lexicographically first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"four-colouring of a planar graph is NP-hard to find, though some four-colouring is found in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"polynomial time. It can be far slower than "},{"code":"minimumColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": on random sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"3-colourable graphs with 2n edges it took about 0.2 s at 1,000 vertices, 2.7 s at 2,000 and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over 100 s at 5,000, where "},{"code":"minimumColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" takes about a millisecond. The search does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"check for task cancellation."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumcoloring()"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Coloring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactColoring.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/ExactColoring.swift#L626"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14ColoringModuleE029lexicographicallyFirstMinimumC0AD0C0VyxGyF","role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"ColoringModule"}],"title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()":{"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumcoloring()","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colour vector (in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its ","type":"text"},{"code":"bipartition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sides (left 0), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colours beside a triangle.","type":"text"}],"title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Coloring","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Graph","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule","type":"topic","title":"ColoringModule","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","kind":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols","type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/Coloring":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A proper colouring of a graph’s vertices by the colours "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<colorCount"},{"type":"text","text":", each of which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used (unless preset colours skip some): the result of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyColoring(strategy:presetColor:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyColoring(order:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":" (JGraphT "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VertexColoringAlgorithm.Coloring"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Graphs.jl "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Coloring"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Coloring"}],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloring","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Coloring"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Coloring","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/Coloring"}}}